From f501bc177631e4dbe621743ffbb73bfff0cd9bd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Ogilby <pgal@google.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 14:28:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Fix RBAC bypass via path parameters

When ignore_path_parameters_in_path_matching is enabled, the router strips path parameters (everything after ';') before matching. However, the RBAC filter's PathMatcher and UriTemplateMatcher did not, leading to a bypass where a path like '/admin;x' bypasses RBAC policies matching '/admin' but is still routed to '/admin'.

This fix exposes ignorePathParametersInPathMatching() on the Route's CommonConfig, and updates RBAC PathMatcher and UriTemplateMatcher to check this config and strip path parameters using a new shared Http::PathUtil helper before evaluating the match.

Fixes GHSA-77x5-xqjg-hprq.

Signed-off-by: Paul Ogilby <pgal@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Kateryna Nezdolii <kateryna.nezdolii@gmail.com>
